    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **salutation** feature: the request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner now returns a read-only `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `title` input property to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema. (The DTOs \u2014 `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto` \u2014 are generated from this spec at build time.)\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the title survives the POST-create \u2192 GET round-trip.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `salutation(owner)` helper and mapped it onto the `salutation` output field. The `title` field maps automatically via MapStruct (present on both request DTO\u2192entity and entity\u2192response DTO).\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column was required for persistence; I updated all four dialects for consistency.\n\nResult: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (POST with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 GET `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
